{"comprehension": {"questions": [{"abstain_if": "", "arms": ["docs"], "because": "Most changes are just doc links; the main risk is pointing to the wrong/newer split module or missing an intended higher-level entry point.", "kind": "docs", "look_at": ["Mathlib/Data/Complex/Basic.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Finset/Defs.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Finsupp/MonomialOrder.lean", "Mathlib/Data/List/Lex.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Matrix/Mul.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Nat/Init.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Option/Defs.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Set/Basic.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Vector3.lean"], "question": "Do the updated path references correspond to real, current files/directories in Mathlib (and not further-renamed modules), and are they the most appropriate canonical pointers for users?"}, {"abstain_if": "", "arms": ["docs", "proof_idiom"], "because": "Some edits adjust headings and phrasing (e.g. changing `##` to `#`, and references from file to directory).", "kind": "style", "look_at": ["Mathlib/Data/Array/Defs.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Option/Defs.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Set/Basic.lean", "Mathlib/Data/Vector3.lean"], "question": "Are the docstring edits consistent with Mathlib style (section headers, wording about where lemmas live, and references to directories vs files)?"}], "summary": "Updates module docstrings and comments across several `Mathlib/Data/*` files to fix stale or moved file references and to better point readers to the current locations of related material."}, "event": "comprehension"}
